  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhaskar Gajula Bhaskar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.4918 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner/A2 seeks to quash the proceedings against him in Crime No.148 of 2019 of Nellore VI Town Police Station, SPSR Nellore District, which was registered against him for the offences under Sections 328, 272, 273, 188 of IPC and Sec.59(i) of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 (for short 'FSS Act, 2006). 2. The allegations against the petitioner briefly are that on 08.08.2019 at 18:30 hours, the S.I of Police along with staff, on credible information proceeded to the house of petitioner situated at NTR Nagar, Nellore, found the petitioner was having gunny bags contained banned tobacco products, seized the same under a cover of panchanama, later he arrested him and registered a case in Crime No.148 of 2019 for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioner while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
